==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
Maxxing out the [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from all chapters can turn this stage into a cakewalk, but it is still beatable if you have all of them from at least Chapter 1 and 2. Despite Cadaver Bear's reach, the Star Peng's low range and high pushing power makes it very easy to lure them into the range of [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] and pick them off. The Shibalien Elite can be disregarded if you have enough Treasures, but timing Chill Cat on them is a bit tricker due to their slightly slower speed. For the Zombies, [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] along with any damage dealing [[Zombie Killer]] can deal with all of them here. You can also use generic backliners like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] to bring Cadaver Bear down to [[Ototo Corps#Holy Blast|Holy Blast]] range, if you don't have any suitable ones. Any [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|Anti-Alien]]/[[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|Anti-Zombie]] Ubers can also remove most of the difficulty from this stage if you happen to own some.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
-

==='''Chapter 3'''===
You can brute-force this stage fairly easily with [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Just save up enough money, then send him out so that he hits the base before sending out a [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] to protect him. He should take care of the enemy base before the second Star Peng even has a chance to make its appearance.

